  <text id="problem-kicker" x="60" y="72" width="300" height="24" font="caption" size="14" color="pink-accent" wrap="false">01  /  THE FRICTION</text>
  <text id="problem-title" x="60" y="110" width="540" height="92" font="heading" size="38" color="text-main" line-height="1.05">Web3 asks users to understand the rails before they feel the value.</text>
  <text id="problem-body" x="60" y="242" width="500" height="270" font="body" size="19" color="text-muted" line-height="1.45">
    <ul bullet="—">
      <li>First-time users must navigate wallet installation, network selection, approval, and signing before the first meaningful action.</li>
      <li>Transactions can feel invisible after clicking “submit,” leaving users unsure whether to wait, retry, or verify a receipt.</li>
      <li>Builders need a human-scale, reviewable way to demonstrate real on-chain participation without hiding the technical truth.</li>
    </ul>
  </text>
